<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chrodegang of Metz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 766</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chrodegang was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a> from 742 until his death in 766 and a leading churchman of the early Carolingian kingdom under Pippin the Short. He wrote a rule for clergy living in community that became a model for cathedral canons, and he introduced Roman chant to the Frankish church. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorze-abbey">Gorze Abbey</a> and briefly headed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorsch">Lorsch</a> Abbey, and is venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chrodegang-of-metz.jpg" alt="Chrodegang of Metz" width="320" height="605" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graoully/Archimatth · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chrodegang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
